     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac effects such as QT prolongation. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg entered as 1000 mg.\n\n2. **You've said you aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, and that matters even more for an order outside the normal range.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. Typical adult dosing is 25\u2013200 mg once daily by mouth.\n- If you send me the confirmed dose and say it comes from the prescriber, I can enter it. For example, I could enter 100 mg by mouth once daily.\n- If the prescriber really does intend 1000 mg, they should enter it themselves and take it through pharmacy review."
      }
     ],
