     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because you've told me you're not the prescriber. The problem is the dose, not whether the request was clear. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum recommended dose of 200 mg, and it could seriously harm the patient.\n\n**What the prescriber can do**\n- Confirm the dose directly with the pharmacy or the ordering system. A licensed prescriber who really intends an unusual dose can enter it and go through the pharmacist's verification.\n- If 1000 mg was a typo, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it. For example, I can enter 100 mg or 200 mg by mouth once daily, if the prescriber confirms that dose.\n\nI'm glad to help with any order that falls within the standard dosing range."
      }
     ],
